          "avatar": "0d3f28d598bdbab72aeb4913c5a43d25ecbd2975"
        },
        "language": "english",
        "review": "I'm a huge fan of other character action games, such as Kingdom Hearts (which this seems to take inspiration from gameplay wise) and Devil May Cry. This is an extremely promising game that I will certainly be keeping an eye on for news and content as development continues.\nPros:\nPlatforming through levels is enjoyable, and levels have hidden secrets for you to find (as well as a tracker in level select to let you know if you missed them).\nCombat is both engaging and satisfying, allowing both ease of entry and rewarding mastery.\nI cannot understate how much I love the aesthetic, both visual and sound design.\n\nCons:\nThe general movement (such as walking and jumping) is in my opinion slightly visually stiff, though this does not extend to the fast paced combat where movement is both fluid and satisfying.\nThe general inability to quickly land and continue attacking enemies while remaining grounded (since the moves that send you to the ground launch enemies away, and the quick chase puts you airborne) means that grounded combos and launchers are not used much without going a bit out of your way to use them.\nThe 3d models being unfortunately relatively low poly (something I am more than okay with, especially given that it makes the game easy to run) sometimes causes them to look a bit goofy in cutscenes, though look great during gameplay. Conversely the 2d artwork is amazing, and the 3d models are on model, with the cutscenes doing a great job of emulating the 2d look with the 3d models most of the time.",
